1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:19,100
In 1970, amidst rising concerns for the health of our ocean, coasts, and inland communities,

2
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:22,900
the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration was created.

3
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:27,660
Among NOAA's new responsibilities was the development of comprehensive programs to protect

4
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:33,460
our ocean, coasts, their ecosystems, and the communities that rely on them.

5
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:37,500
Essential stewardship initiatives arose from these programs, including protection of

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,700
our nation's fisheries and marine mammal populations, restoring ecosystems impacted

7
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:50,540
by oil and chemical spills, and a world-class weather service protecting life and property.

8
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:55,540
Over the last 50 years, NOAA's stewardship efforts have greatly expanded.

9
00:00:55,540 --> 00:01:01,240
NOAA scientists monitor and document the many ways our world is changing around us.

10
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,900
We face unprecedented challenges, and NOAA remains at the forefront of addressing them.

11
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:13,300
Through a national marine debris program, citizen science and education programs, and many others,

12
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:18,540
NOAA is actively engaging the public and meeting the challenges affecting our ecosystems and

13
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:21,620
the communities that depend on them.

14
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:26,760
From monitoring and protecting freshwater, marine, and coastal ecosystems, including

15
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:31,160
coral reefs and estuaries, to conserving and restoring them for the public to enjoy

16
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:36,440
and benefit from for generations to come, stewardship is the foundation that NOAA will

17
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:40,920
continue to build upon for our country's future.

18
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:43,200
We look forward to that future.

19
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:48,280
To meet the challenges of the next 50 years, NOAA must ensure that our communities and ecosystems

20
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,960
remain resilient.

21
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:57,240
We're embracing new technologies and leveraging our nation's greatest asset, our youth.

22
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:02,080
We must prepare and inspire our leaders of tomorrow, and support the educators and

23
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:06,400
community leaders who teach and nurture imagination.

24
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,960
Those of the next generation are the leaders of stewardship for the future.

25
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:17,640
The success of NOAA's stewardship initiatives demands that we embrace our country's diversity.

26
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:23,520
We must reflect, understand, and respond to the broad range of communities, partners,

27
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,280
and stakeholders we serve.

28
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:31,040
Together, we'll maintain healthy ecosystems, communities, and economies that are resilient

29
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,120
in the face of change.

